You are a trained observer comparing the prepared presentations of several entrepreneur
pitches. Each clip below is one pitch's prepared presentation, cut before any investor
questioning. The clips are labelled {{ labels | join(", ") }}.

RULES
1. Watch every clip in full, with sound, before ranking anything.
2. For each dimension below, put the clips in a strict order from the one that shows the
   MOST of that dimension to the one that shows the LEAST.
3. No ties. Every clip appears exactly once in every order. When two clips are close, decide
   which shows more, and say in the note that they were close.
4. Judge each dimension on its own definition. A clip can be first on one dimension and last
   on another. Do not form one overall impression and repeat it.
5. Judge only what is seen and heard in the clips. Do not judge the business idea, do not use
   outside knowledge of the people or companies, and do not guess what happened afterwards.
6. Do not give scores. Give only the order, and one note of about 25 words per dimension
   saying what separates the top of the order from the bottom.
7. If missing or unusable founder speech or view of the presenters prevents the judgement on
   a dimension, still place the clip, last on that dimension, and say so in the note.
8. The definitions below were written for rating one presentation at a time. Where they
   mention a rating, a score or a number, read it as more or less of the dimension. Where a
   definition says to apply the shared protocol or to mark a clip uncodable, follow these
   rules instead.

DIMENSIONS
{% for e in entries %}
### {{ e.id }}
Definition: {{ e.definition }}
Include if: {{ e.include_if }}
Exclude if: {{ e.exclude_if }}
{% endfor %}

Return one JSON object with `rankings` (one item per dimension: its code, the order as a list
of clip labels, and the note) and `notes` (anything a reviewer must know; empty if nothing).
